Actually, yellow lights are the only ones of those that blind you.  Fog
clouds just surround you.  And floating eyes... are probably your problem.

If you attack a floating eye at close range, its gaze paralyzes you.  Then
a newt or something will walk up and beat you into a bloody pulp while you
stand there paralyzed -- this is when you'll get a "killed by a newt while
helpless" gravestone.  This has been the cause of countless deaths for
most of us :)  So don't attack a floating eye in melee.  Either zap it
with attack spells (as a wizard) or attack wands (if you have them), or
throw rocks or daggers at it, or shoot it with arrows.  Also, if you're a
knight, you can (a)pply your lance from 2 squares back.

Another way you may be blinded is by a magic trap.  You should get the
message "you step on a magic trap" and then be surrounded by monsters.
Read the messages carefully -- once you figure out how you're dying,
you'll start to develop methods to avoid it.



